  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LBN004N Lebanon ACJR 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description promeva:title="Description (English)" promeva:type="104" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The escalation of hostilities in Lebanon since late February 2026 has triggered large-scale displacement and rapidly increasing humanitarian needs. Airstrikes across Beirut&#x2019;s southern suburbs, the Beqaa Valley and southern Lebanon have caused civilian casualties and widespread infrastructure damage. Through a multisectoral 6-month emergency response CARE and partners will support crisis-affected and displaced individuals in Lebanon.

The intervention is informed by CARE&#x2019;s Rapid Needs Assessment and Rapid Gender Analysis and builds on the complementary expertise of CARE, HAND and LECORVAW in FSL, WASH, and Gender and Protection. CARE, HAND and LECORVAW propose a lifesaving food, protection and WASH response with protection mainstreamed to 26,000 conflict-affected populations in BML and Baalbek-Hermel. Food security needs will be addressed through the distribution of ready-to-eat meals and food parcels by CARE in BML targeting 15,000 vulnerable individuals including women and girls, children, older persons, people with disabilities, pregnant and lactating women, GBV survivors, refugees and migrant workers, who face heightened risks during displacement. WASH needs will be addressed through hygiene kit distribution and support to collective shelters through comprehensive WASH packages (water trucking, desludging, minor repairs, etc.) implemented by HAND&amp;CARE in Baalbek-Hermel targeting 9,000 individuals. Protection risks, particularly affecting women, girls and LGBTQI+, will be addressed through the provision of dignity kits, GBV awareness and referral pathways, as well as PSEA and AAP awareness activities implemented by LECORVAW and CARE in BML targeting 2,000 individuals. Protection mainstreaming will be ensured across the response, and all activities will adhere to recognised humanitarian standards, including Sphere standards and relevant sector guidance.</narrative>
  </description>
